      "evidence": "Step 2.1 says: “The edge bound in [L1] makes each forbidden family small enough that, after all such deletions, at least s vertices remain in A_i.” But [L1] supplies only a total edge bound for each original pair. The proof defines neither the heavy-vertex thresholds nor the deletion sets, gives no aggregate bound over the l-1 prior/future constraints, and provides no construction that can enforce a condition against an “eventually chosen” D_j. Thus it does not establish either survivor availability or the directional conclusion used in 3.1.",
