      "evidence": "Step 4.1 asserts “w>=q/ell>=epsilon^2 m.” The second inequality is false under its preceding definitions q=ceil(epsilon ceil(m)) and ell=ceil(epsilon^{-1}). For epsilon=3/250 and m=27000, ell=84 and q=324, so q/ell=27/7<486/125=epsilon^2 m. The available bound ell<=epsilon^{-2} gives q/ell>=epsilon^3 m, which would suffice for the later target, but the written computation is false.",
